  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: origin credentials sent to an HTTP proxy\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-86414.patch: only react to 407 responses with\n       Proxy-Authenticate during CONNECT, ignore 401 WWW-Authenticate in\n       lib/http_proxy.c\n     - CVE-2026-86414\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: IMAP command injection with CRLF conversion\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-87864.patch: deny APPEND when line-end\n       conversion makes the upload size unknown in lib/imap.c\n     - CVE-2026-87864\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free after a failed FTP wildcard listing\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-92388.patch: stop overwriting the write callback\n       and data, route listing data to the parser in lib/sendf.c, lib/ftp.c,\n       lib/ftp.h and lib/ftplistparser.{c,h}\n     - CVE-2026-92388\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: TFTP transfer direction confusion\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-92389.patch: verify the transfer direction in\n       lib/tftp.c\n     - CVE-2026-92389\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: stack overflow freeing deeply nested MIME structures\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-92391.patch: free mime handles non-recursively\n       in lib/mime.c\n     - CVE-2026-92391",
